The MIT terms above cover the code: everything under `scripts/` and the
configuration template.

The data products — the gold-standard label table and the manifests under
`data/`, and every table under `results/` — are released under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC-BY-4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Use them freely, including
commercially, with attribution to this repository and to the accompanying
publication.

The figures under `figures/` are likewise CC-BY-4.0.

The underlying genome assemblies are not redistributed here. They are the NCBI
type-material collection and remain under NCBI's own terms; `data/genome_manifest.tsv`
lists the accessions needed to retrieve them.
